# Static deployment baseline

`npm run build` creates `dist/` with the rendered pages plus these generated operational files:

- a starter `privacy/` page; replace its legal placeholders before publishing;
- `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml`, derived from `content/*.md` and `meta.base_url`;
- `.well-known/security.txt` when `site.md` contains a valid `contact.email`;
- `_headers` for Netlify, Cloudflare Pages and compatible static hosts;
- `.htaccess` for Apache hosts.

The header files configure a restrictive Content Security Policy, HSTS, referrer and
permissions policies, clickjacking protection, MIME sniffing protection, and caching for
static assets. Do not delete them from the deployed `dist/` directory. If the hosting
provider uses Caddy, nginx, a CDN or another server, translate the same headers into that
provider's configuration and verify them over HTTPS in production.

The generated CSP intentionally permits outbound HTTPS connections only for an explicitly
configured form gateway. Keep all fonts, scripts, styles and ordinary images local. If a
site needs a third-party integration, document it in the privacy notice and update the
CSP deliberately rather than weakening it globally.

Set a real `meta.base_url`, site-specific `meta.site_title`, and description before
publishing. Pages can set `noindex: true` or `sitemap: false` in front matter when they
must not be discoverable.
